# Supabase SQL conventions

- File name `NNNN_<module>_<doctype>.sql`; ranges: 0000-0099 framework, 0100 setup, 0200 stock masters, 0300 accounts,
  0400 selling, 0500 buying, 0600 stock txns, 0700 manufacturing, 0800 projects, 0900 assets, 1000+ reports/perf.
- Table = ERPNext doctype in snake_case (`sales_invoice`, child `sales_invoice_item`). Keep ERPNext fieldnames.
- Base columns on every tenant table: `id uuid pk default gen_random_uuid()`, `org_id uuid not null references organizations(id) on delete cascade`,
  `created_at/created_by/updated_at/updated_by`. Transactional docs add `company_id`, `name` (null until submit),
  `naming_series`, `docstatus smallint check (docstatus in (0,1,2))`, `status`, `amended_from`, `posting_date`.
- Child tables: `parent_id uuid not null references <parent>(id) on delete cascade`, `idx int`, `org_id`.
- Money/qty: `numeric(21,9)`. Enum-like fields: `text` + `check` with ERPNext labels verbatim.
- Every migration ends with:
  ```sql
  alter table <t> enable row level security; alter table <t> force row level security;
  -- select/insert/update/delete policies using (select app.has_perm(org_id,'<DocType>','<action>'))
  insert into doctype_meta (...) on conflict do update ...;
  insert into role_permissions (...) on conflict do nothing;   -- from ERPNext doctype JSON permissions
  ```
- Child-table policies delegate to the parent via `exists (select 1 from <parent> p where p.id = parent_id)`.
- Ledger tables (`gl_entry`, `stock_ledger_entry`, `payment_ledger_entry`, `bin`): select policies only; writes only from
  `security definer` functions in schema `app`.
- `security definer` functions: `set search_path = app, public, pg_temp`, first statement checks `app.has_perm(...)`,
  lock the header row `for update`, raise with `using errcode = 'P0001', message = '<machine_key>: <human text>'`.
- Every new `app.*` function: `revoke execute ... from public, anon, authenticated` then grant only what is needed
  (Supabase's role-level default privileges otherwise grant it to anon). `app` is not exposed; RPC entry points are
  `public.<fn>` `security invoker` wrappers over the `app` implementation.
- Idempotent DDL (`if not exists`, `drop policy if exists`), no `execute_sql` DDL against prod, never disable RLS.
- Indexes: `(org_id, name)`, `(org_id, company_id, docstatus, posting_date desc)` + the ledger indexes in
  `docs/architecture/02-database-conventions.md`.
- Add a pgTAP test under `supabase/tests/` for each posting function and an RLS isolation test for each table.
